messages:
maria: Hey — pushed a tiny Next starter that wires up the eval harness + a lightweight LangChain example. Trying to keep it minimal (SSG-friendly) and using the JS SDK for hosted calls. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/examples/pull/42 :sparkles:

alex: Nice! Quick note — I ran the example and hit inconsistent retry behavior. The Python example retries auth-refresh on 401, but the JS SDK just fails. Repro: run `yarn start` then call /api/generate with a revoked token.

sam: That sounds like a gap in the JS client. We used the node SDK's auto-refresh in internal infra but didn't upstream the token-refresh middleware to the public package. Workaround: catch 401 and call refresh endpoint then retry once. Eg:
```js
async function fetchWithRefresh(req) {
  let res = await client.generate(req);
  if (res.status === 401) {
    await refreshToken();
    res = await client.generate(req);
  }
  return res;
}
```

jordan: Also saw a flaky build when using SSG + streaming responses. Next tries to serialize the streaming Readable and fails during `next export`. For starter I switched to client-side fetch for streaming and left SSG for non-streaming paths. Might be worth documenting tradeoffs in the starter README.

ci-bot: :x: CI failed on examples/next-starter -> test/integration/eval-harness.test.js (timeout)

maria: Thanks — I'm going to: 1) add a short note in README about streaming vs SSG, 2) add a tiny retry wrapper in the example, and 3) open a follow-up issue to add token-refresh middleware to the JS SDK.

alex: If you want, I can draft the SDK middleware. It should be pretty small — intercept responses, if 401 call provided refresh function, then replay request. Need to decide if refresh is builtin or passed by user (env var vs callback).

sam: Prefer explicit callback in SDK config for security and host-specific flows. Example config: `new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, onRefresh: async () => fetch('/refresh').then(r => r.json()) })`.

maria: Perfect. I'll merge the starter with the local wrapper so unblock onboarding. Created issue #128 to track upstream SDK change. Tagging @alex for the middleware. :+1:

jordan: One more gotcha for the README — note that the eval harness uses short prompt sets by default; explain how to swap to a larger eval set (and add a CI flag so runs don't time out).

maria: Good call. I'll add `EVAL_QUICK=true` to CI matrix and explain in docs. Thanks team!
